@page "/docs/components/spinner"
@using Blaizio.Docs.Examples.Spinner
<PageTitle>Spinner - Blaizio</PageTitle>

<div class="typeset typeset-docs space-y-10">
    <header class="docs-page-header space-y-2.5">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Spinner</h1>
            <DocBadges Slug="spinner" />
        </div>
        <p>The library's single loading indicator, so a busy state looks the same in a button, a badge, an input group addon or an empty region. It renders with <code>role="status"</code> and a "Loading" label by default, so screen readers announce it without extra markup.</p>
    </header>

    <UsageBlock Example="typeof(SpinnerUsageExample)" />

    <ExamplesHeading />

    <Demo Title="Size"
          Description="Size it with a `size-*` class through `Class`. The default is `size-4`."
          Example="typeof(SpinnerSizeExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Color"
          Description="The spinner draws in `currentColor`, so a `text-*` class tints it."
          Example="typeof(SpinnerColorExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Button"
          Description="Add `data-icon` so the button trims the padding on that edge, and disable the button while the work runs."
          Example="typeof(SpinnerButtonExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Badge" Example="typeof(SpinnerBadgeExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Input group"
          Description="As an inline-end addon, the spinner shows that the value is being checked."
          Example="typeof(SpinnerInputGroupExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Empty"
          Description="Composed with `BzEmpty`, it marks a whole region as busy."
          Example="typeof(SpinnerEmptyExample)" />

    <Demo Title="RTL"
          Description="Inside a right-to-left `DirectionProvider`, a spinner marked with `data-icon` moves to the opposite edge of the button, along with the padding adjustment."
          Example="typeof(SpinnerRtlExample)" />
</div>
